# Optional. scripts/battlenet finds or installs Battle.net by itself; copy
# to ~/.config/modern/battlenet.env (gitignored) only to pin one install
# or runner. Prefer BATTLENET_EXE — Steam Non-Steam AppID launch is
# unreliable on Linux.
# Quote paths that contain spaces.

# Absolute path to Battle.net Launcher.exe inside the Proton prefix:
BATTLENET_EXE="$HOME/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/compatdata/<id>/pfx/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Battle.net/Battle.net Launcher.exe"
WINEPREFIX="$HOME/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/compatdata/<id>/pfx"

# Directory containing the `proton` binary. Leave unset and install.sh's
# private GE-Proton11-12 is used
# (~/.local/share/modern/proton/GE-Proton11-12-x86_64). That tree stays
# outside compatibilitytools.d so Steam does not GPU-probe it.
# PROTONPATH="$HOME/.local/share/modern/proton/GE-Proton11-12-x86_64"

# Optional fallback only (often fails with "game configuration is not available"):
# STEAM_APPID=

# Already defaulted by scripts/battlenet — override only if needed:
# PROTON_ENABLE_WAYLAND=0
# WINE_SIMULATE_WRITECOPY=1
# AMD_VULKAN_ICD=RADV
# BATTLENET_IN_PROCESS_GPU=1
# BATTLENET_ARGS=--disable-gpu
# BATTLENET_HDR=1
